{
 "_format": [
  "Names typed in Latin letters -> a card's script. Casual phonetic typing (as in WhatsApp), not ISO 15919. Shared by iOS, web and Android.",
  "Each run of ASCII letters is one word; everything else passes through unchanged.",
  "1. Case: an all-capitals word is lowercased; otherwise only its first letter is (Title case ignored). Capitals left inside a word mark retroflex (T, D, N, L, R, Sh).",
  "2. words[lowercased word], when present, is the whole answer for that word.",
  "3. Tokens, greedy longest match left to right (longest key first, up to the longest key in the script). At each length try the text as typed, then lowercased; for each, look in syllables, then consonants, then vowels. A letter matching nothing passes through.",
  "4. Emit. vowel token: after a consonant token it becomes signs[v] (signs.a is the inherent vowel, \"\"), except a word-final \"a\" after a consonant, which becomes endA; anywhere else (start of word, after a vowel or syllable) it is vowels[v].",
  "   consonant token C: its letter is initial[C] when it is the word's first token, subjoined[C] when the token before it is a consonant, else consonants[C] (each map optional, falling back to consonants).",
  "   Then by what follows: a vowel -> letter + sign as above. A consonant or syllable -> medial[C] if present (replaces the letter, no virama), else letter + virama. Nothing (word end) -> final[C] if present (replaces the letter), else letter + finalA.",
  "   syllable token: syllables[S] as is (a consonant already carrying its vowel, e.g. kri -> കൃ); what follows it starts afresh.",
  "   Except: a word-final y straight after a consonant is read as the vowel signs.y when the script has one (Parvathy -> പർവതി).",
  "Consonant keys may be clusters (ksh, shn, nj ...) whose value is a ready conjunct; values may begin with an anusvara (\"ंज\"), which simply follows the previous syllable.",
  "Tests: translit-tests.json beside this file, {script: [[latin, native], ...]}, must pass on every platform."
 ],
